{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfrzihRCBksGVMafZBpsX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I implemented `cachelib/lru.py` to the spec and added tests in `tests/test_lru.py`. All 12 tests pass.\n\nThe cache is built on `OrderedDict` and covers everything in `SPEC.md`:\n- **TTL:** it uses the injectable clock, and an entry counts as expired once the clock reaches its expiry time (`now >= expires_at`).\n- **`put`:** it resets the TTL on every put.\n- **Expired `get`:** it counts one miss and one expiration, not an eviction.\n\nThe spec doesn't say whether `__contains__` should remove an expired entry, so it doesn't. It returns `False` for an expired entry but leaves the entry in place and leaves the stats alone. A later `get` then removes it and counts the expiration.\n\nExpired entries stay in the cache until something removes them, so they count toward `len()` and capacity. A `put` over capacity evicts the least recently used entry even if an expired entry is sitting in the cache.\n\nThe tests cover invalid capacity, LRU eviction order, update and recency behaviour, `delete`, the stats counters, and TTL handling with a fake clock."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5002,"cache_read_input_tokens":46417,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5002},"output_tokens":376,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a23cffc9-c2cb-43ee-a6f1-1f2da2a53621","uuid":"f14b1f82-ea84-4bd8-bd18-dc2842aaba2e","timestamp":"2026-10-09T16:41:30.163Z","request_id":"req_011CfrzihAp81xha8ChsN7HY"}
